{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"The \"agents\" concept in pi isn't a standard directory like `~/.pi/agent/agents/`. The task mentions \"agents/\" as a directory where \"think/research/exporter agent frontmatter\" would be written. But this is task9's job, not task3. For task3, the requirement says:\n\n> 职责 3 `DeployRickCustomizations()`：**task3 创建仓库侧 `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` 占位文件 + 目录骨架**（实际门禁校验逻辑 tasks.json 可解析/zombie/commit_hash 由 task8 填充），`DeployRickCustomizations` 幂等复制 rick-gates + rick skills 到 `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`；**think/research/exporter agent 文件本 task 不写、完全留给 task9**（避免 task3 占位文件被 task9 幂等跳过）\n\nSo task3:\n1. Creates repository-side `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` placeholder file + directory skeleton.\n2. `DeployRickCustomizations` idempotently copies rick-gates + rick skills to `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`.\n3. think/research/exporter agent files NOT written in this task (left to task9).\n\nWait, re-reading more carefully: \"`DeployRickCustomizations` 幂等复制 rick-gates + rick skills 到 `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`\"\n\nHmm, so the rick-gates extension goes to `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/` and rick skills go... let me re-read.\n\nThe task goal says:\n> 3. **安装并更新 rick 自有定制（hook/skill/agent）**：新增 `DeployRickCustomizations()`，把 rick-gates hook 扩展、think/research/exporter agent frontmatter、rick skills 落盘到 `~/.rick/pi/agent/`（agents/、extensions/、skills/）\n\nSo:\n- rick-gates hook extension → `~/.rick/pi/agent/extensions/rick-gates/`\n- think/research/exporter agent frontmatter → `~/.rick/pi/agent/agents/`\n- rick skills → `~/.rick/pi/agent/skills/`\n\nBut KR 2 says: \"task3 创建仓库侧 `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` 占位文件 + 目录骨架（实际门禁校验逻辑 tasks.json 可解析/zombie/commit_hash 由 task8 填充），`DeployRickCustomizations` 幂等复制 rick-gates + rick skills 到 `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`；**think/research/exporter agent 文件本 task 不写、完全留给 task9**\"\n\nHmm, \"幂等复制 rick-gates + rick skills 到 `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`\" — this is a bit ambiguous. It seems to say: copy rick-gates (the extension) AND rick skills to `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`? That doesn't quite make sense. Let me re-read the goal more carefully.\n\nActually re-reading: the goal says three sub-directories (agents/, extensions/, skills/). But KR2 specifically says \"幂等复制 rick-gates + rick skills 到 `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`\". \n\nI think there might be a slight inconsistency, but the key checkable requirement from the test script (task3.py) is:\n- `DeployRickCustomizations` symbol exists in env source.\n- `internal/env` has IsPIReady, CheckPIInstalled, CheckEcosystemExtensions, CheckRickAgents, CheckRickHooks.\n- `type RuntimeEnv interface` with DeployCustomizations, CheckReady methods.\n- `piEnv` implementation.\n\nThe test script doesn't check the exact paths of deployment. But the doing_check (format check) and the \"golden output\" requirement are important.\n\nActually, wait — the more important thing is:\n1. `CheckRickAgents` should check agents directory readiness, `CheckRickHooks` checks the rick-gates hook extension, `CheckRickAgents` checks... hmm.\n\nLet me focus on the concrete requirements and make reasonable decisions:\n\n**职责 3 DeployRickCustomizations()**:\n- Create repo-side `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` placeholder + directory skeleton.\n- Idempotently copy rick-gates (extension) to `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`.\n- Copy rick skills to `runtime.AgentDir()/skills/` (rick skills = the `.rick/skills/*` directories? or a subset?).\n- think/research/exporter agent files NOT written in this task.\n\nLet me think about what \"rick skills\" means. There's `.rick/skills/` with skill directories (each has SKILL.md?). Actually let me check the structure of .rick/skills — they have directories like `check_mechanism_skill/`, and the prompt references `skill.md`? Let me check.\n\nActually the skills listed in the task prompt use names like `check-mechanism`, `verify_go_changes_skill`, etc. Let me look at the .rick/skills directory structure to understand what to copy.\n\nLet me check what's inside .rick/skills and .rick/loops directories."}}
