{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now I have a thorough understanding. Let me verify the current build passes and check what pi docs say about hooks. Let me also check the `bash-spawn-hook.ts` example which is a \"hook\" — actually \"hook\" in pi is the \"spawnHook\" concept. Let me check what \"hook 扩展\" means. The task says \"rick-gates hook 扩展\". \n\nActually looking at the example `bash-spawn-hook.ts`:\n- It's an extension that hooks into bash spawn. \n\nThe task says: \"把 rick-gates hook 扩展...落盘到 ~/.rick/pi/agent/（agents/、extensions/、skills/）\"\n\nSo rick-gates is an extension (hook type). It goes into `extensions/rick-gates/`. The \"hook\" refers to the kind of extension (spawnHook for gating commands).\n\nFor task3, I need to:\n1. Create repo-side `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` placeholder + directory skeleton.\n2. `DeployRickCustomizations` copies rick-gates extension + rick skills to `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/` (and skills to `runtime.AgentDir()/skills/`).\n\nWait, let me re-read KR2 exactly:\n\n> 职责 3 `DeployRickCustomizations()`：**task3 创建仓库侧 `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` 占位文件 + 目录骨架**（实际门禁校验逻辑 tasks.json 可解析/zombie/commit_hash 由 task8 填充），`DeployRickCustomizations` 幂等复制 rick-gates + rick skills 到 `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`；**think/research/exporter agent 文件本 task 不写、完全留给 task9**（避免 task3 占位文件被 task9 幂等跳过）\n\nSo:\n- Repo-side `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` placeholder + directory skeleton (rick-gates lives under `.rick/skills/rick-gates/`).\n- `DeployRickCustomizations` copies \"rick-gates + rick skills\" to `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`.\n\nHmm. This is confusing. Let me re-read again carefully:\n\n\"`DeployRickCustomizations` 幂等复制 rick-gates + rick skills 到 `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`\"\n\nI think this means: copy rick-gates (the extension, from `.rick/skills/rick-gates/`) to `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`, AND copy rick skills to `runtime.AgentDir()/skills/`. The text is just a bit compressed.\n\nActually wait. The goal (from 任务目标 section) says clearly:\n\n> 3. **安装并更新 rick 自有定制（hook/skill/agent）**：新增 `DeployRickCustomizations()`，把 rick-gates hook 扩展、think/research/exporter agent frontmatter、rick skills 落盘到 `~/.rick/pi/agent/`（agents/、extensions/、skills/）——rick 全局方法...作为 builder method 的固定前缀（task5），不单独落盘 `APPEND_SYSTEM.md`\n\nSo the three sub-dirs are:\n- `agents/` → think/research/exporter agent frontmatter (task9)\n- `extensions/` → rick-gates hook 扩展\n- `skills/` → rick skills\n\nAnd KR2 refines: task3 does rick-gates (extension) + rick skills; task9 does agents.\n\nSo my `DeployRickCustomizations` should:\n1. Copy rick-gates extension to `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`.\n2. Copy rick skills to `runtime.AgentDir()/skills/`.\n\nThe source of rick-gates is `.rick/skills/rick-gates/` (repo-side). The source of rick skills is `.rick/skills/*`.\n\nBut wait — what's the exact content of the rick-gates extension? It's a \"hook 扩展\". pi extensions are `.ts` files in `~/.pi/agent/extensions/`. For a \"subdirectory\" structure: `~/.pi/agent/extensions/*/index.ts`.\n\nSo `extensions/rick-gates/index.ts` would be the extension entry. But the task says \"task3 创建仓库侧 `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` 占位文件 + 目录骨架\" and \"实际门禁校验逻辑 tasks.json 可解析/zombie/commit_hash 由 task8 填充\".\n\nSo for task3, I just need:\n- `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` placeholder (the actual gating logic comes in task8).\n- `DeployRickCustomizations` copies the rick-gates directory to `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`.\n\nBut wait, helper.py is a Python file, not a .ts extension. Hmm. The \"hook\" might be a script, not a pi .ts extension. Let me reconsider.\n\nActually the spec says \"门禁 → 下沉 pi hook/脚本\". So the gate is a \"hook/脚本\" (hook/script). The rick-gates could be:\n- A pi extension (hook, .ts) that intercepts bash commands and runs gate scripts.\n- The gate logic itself (helper.py) that does the tasks.json parse/zombie/commit_hash checks.\n\nFor task3, the placeholder is just the skeleton. The actual content (gating logic) is task8.\n\nLet me think about what's minimal and correct for task3:\n1. `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` — placeholder Python script (skeleton, no real logic).\n2. `.rick/skills/rick-gates/` directory skeleton (maybe a README or index).\n\nAnd `DeployRickCustomizations`:\n1. Ensures `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/` exists and copies the repo-side rick-gates files there (idempotent).\n2. Ensures `runtime.AgentDir()/skills/` exists and copies rick skills there (idempotent).\n\nNow, what about the pi skills format? Rick skills use `skill.md` (lowercase) but pi expects `SKILL.md`. Hmm, but the task doesn't require me to convert. Actually wait — the deployment target is `~/.rick/pi/agent/skills/`. pi loads skills from there. If rick skills use `skill.md`, pi won't discover them. But this is a \"copy\" operation for task3; the actual semantics of how pi uses them may be refined later.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The task says \"rick skills 落盘到 ~/.rick/pi/agent/（...skills/）\". The simplest interpretation: copy the `.rick/skills/*` directories to `runtime.AgentDir()/skills/*`.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: the rick-gates directory will be created under `.rick/skills/rick-gates/`. So when copying \"rick skills\", should I also copy rick-gates to skills/? No — rick-gates goes to extensions/, not skills/.\n\nHmm wait, actually re-reading again: \"`DeployRickCustomizations` 幂等复制 rick-gates + rick skills 到 `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`\".\n\nMaybe this literally means: copy both rick-gates AND rick skills into `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`? That seems odd. Let me look at whether there's a plan/task3.md file that has more detail."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_il5CcMFrjJYHqz53TRyo2735","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && cat .rick/jobs/job_35/plan/task3.md 2>/dev/null | head -200"}}}}
