tself (helper.py) that does the tasks.json parse/zombie/commit_hash checks.\n\nFor task3, the placeholder is just the skeleton. The actual content (gating logic) is task8.\n\nLet me think about what's minimal and correct for task3:\n1. `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` — placeholder Python script (skeleton, no real logic).\n2. `.rick/skills/rick-gates/` directory skeleton (maybe a README or index).\n\nAnd `DeployRickCustomizations`:\n1. Ensures `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/` exists and copies the repo-side rick-gates files there (idempotent).\n2. Ensures `runtime.AgentDir()/skills/` exists and copies rick skills there (idempotent).\n\nNow, what about the pi skills format? Rick skills use `skill.md` (lowercase) but pi expects `SKILL.md`. Hmm, but the task doesn't require me to convert. Actually wait — the deployment target is `~/.rick/pi/agent/skills/`. pi loads skills from there. If rick skills use `skill.md`, pi won't discover them. But this is a \"copy\" operation for task3; the actual semantics of how pi uses them may be refined later.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The task says \"rick skills 落盘到 ~/.rick/pi/agent/（...skills/）\". The simplest interpretation: copy the `.rick/skills/*` directories to `runtime.AgentDir()/skills/*`.\n\nBut there's a subtlety: the rick-gates directory will be created under `.rick/skills/rick-gates/`. So when copying \"rick skills\", should I also copy rick-gates to skills/? No — rick-gates goes to extensions/, not skills/.\n\nHmm wait, actually re-reading again: \"`DeployRickCustomizations` 幂等复制 rick-gates + rick skills 到 `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`\".\n\nMaybe this literally means: copy both rick-gates AND rick skills into `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`? That seems odd. Let me look at whether there's a plan/task3.md file that has more detail.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_il5CcMFrjJYHqz53TRyo2735","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdi