iInstall_*`, `TestCurrentTheme_*`, `TestSetTheme_PreservesOtherFields`, `TestBootstrapAgentSettings_*`, `TestPurgeTokyoNight_*`, `TestDeployRickCustomizations`.\n  - Test helpers: `writeFakePi`, `writeFakeBin`, `setupPiSettings`, `setupLegacyPiSettings`, `readManagedSettings` (copied).\n\n**internal/cmd tests** (updates):\n- `tools_init_pi_test.go` — mostly empty now (the migrated tests moved to env). But there might be a `TestInitPiCommand` test that runs the command? Let me check if there's a command-level test. Actually the current tools_init_pi_test.go only has the helper function tests (all migrated). So after migration, `tools_init_pi_test.go` can be deleted or kept with a thin command smoke test.\n- `tools_theme_test.go` — keeps `runThemeList`/`runThemeSet`/`customThemeNames` tests, but helper functions `setupPiSettings`/`readManagedSettings` need to use `env.PiSettingsPath()` and `env.CurrentTheme()`. So I'll copy the helpers into tools_theme_test.go and update references.\n\nWait, `tools_theme_test.go` uses `currentTheme()` (→ env.CurrentTheme), `readManagedSettings` (uses piSettingsPath → env.PiSettingsPath), `setupPiSettings` (writes settings.json directly, doesn't use piSettingsPath but sets HOME). Let me check: `setupPiSettings` writes to `filepath.Join(home, \".rick\", \"pi\", \"agent\", \"settings.json\")` directly and sets HOME. It doesn't call `piSettingsPath`. But `readManagedSettings` calls `piSettingsPath()`.\n\nSo in tools_theme_test.go, I need to change `currentTheme()` → `env.CurrentTheme()` and `readManagedSettings` helper to use `env.PiSettingsPath()`. And `runThemeSet`/`runThemeList`/`customThemeNames` remain in cmd (they're tested in cmd package).\n\nActually wait — `customThemeNames()` currently uses `runtime.AgentDir()` directly. It stays in cmd. But `runThemeList` also calls `currentTheme()` (→ env.CurrentTheme) and `piListContains` (→ env.PiListContains). So the cmd `runThemeList`/`runThemeSet` need to be updated to call env.\n\nLet me