{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"I have the baseline output. Note the HOME dir is randomized (mktemp), so for a byte-identical diff I'd need to normalize the path. But the important thing is the output structure/format is identical. I'll do a diff with normalized paths later.\n\nThe baseline output:\n```\n⚠️  rick's managed pi runtime missing — installing self-contained pi under <HOME>/.rick/pi/agent/runtime (matching global v0.84.1) ...\n✅ rick pi runtime ready: <HOME>/.rick/pi/agent/runtime/node_modules/.bin/pi (v0.84.1) (newly installed)\n✅ pi agent dir ready: <HOME>/.rick/pi/agent (hideThinkingBlock=true)\n✅ pi subagent extension ready\n✅ pi web-access extension ready\n✅ tokyo-night purged from managed config (theme/packages)\n✅ verification: all required extensions registered\n✅ verification: theme rick active\n✅ pi environment ready\n```\n\nInteresting — \"matching global v0.84.1\" appears because the fake pi's `--version` returns \"0.84.1\", so `ensurePI` matches that version. Wait, but actually the `piVersion(p)` uses `exec.LookPath(\"pi\")` to find the global pi and get its version. With the fake pi on PATH returning \"0.84.1\", it matches. Good.\n\nNow let me plan the implementation. I have all the info I need. Let me now write the env package.\n\nLet me create the directory and files. First, move the themes.\n\nPlan of files in `internal/env/`:\n1. `env.go` — package doc, RuntimeEnv interface, piEnv, NewPiEnv, Ensure() orchestration.\n2. `pi.go` — EnsurePI, InstallManagedPI, RequireNodeForPiInstall, PiVersion, PiCommand.\n3. `extensions.go` — RequiredExtensions, EnsureNpmExtension, PiListContains, VerifyExtensions.\n4. `settings.go` — TokyoNightPkg, TokyoNightThemes, BootstrapAgentSettings, EnsureRickTheme, EnsureHideThinkingBlock, PurgeTokyoNight, ContainsString, CurrentTheme, SetTheme, PiSettingsPath, LegacyPiSettingsPath, ExtensionManagedByRick + theme embed + WriteEmbeddedTheme.\n5. `customizations.go` — DeployRickCustomizations.\n6. `check.go` — IsPIReady, CheckReady, CheckPIInstalled, CheckEcosystemExtensions, CheckRickAgents, CheckRickHooks.\n7. `themes/*.json` — moved from internal/cmd/themes/.\n\nLet me now write the code. I'll port the functions with minimal changes (just rename to exported, change `runtime.X` references to stay the same since env imports runtime, and change internal calls to exported names).\n\nLet me be careful about the exact output strings.\n\nLet me start writing. First, `env.go`.\n\nActually, I realize I need to decide the exact structure of `Ensure()`. Let me design it as the verbatim port of `runInitPi()`, with a silent `DeployRickCustomizations()` call added at the end (before \"✅ pi environment ready\"). And it returns error only on fatal (pi unavailable).\n\nLet me write the files now.\n\nFor `piEnv`:\n```go\ntype piEnv struct{}\n\nfunc NewPiEnv() *piEnv { return &piEnv{} }\n\nfunc (e *piEnv) Ensure() error { return Ensure() }\nfunc (e *piEnv) DeployCustomizations() error { return DeployRickCustomizations() }\nfunc (e *piEnv) CheckReady() []string { return CheckReady() }\n```\n\nFor the interface:\n```go\ntype RuntimeEnv interface {\n    Ensure() error\n    DeployCustomizations() error\n    CheckReady() []string\n}\n```\n\nNow, `Ensure()`:\n```go\nfunc Ensure() error {\n    // Step 0: node/npm prerequisite\n    if !runtime.FileExists(runtime.RuntimeBin()) {\n        if err := RequireNodeForPiInstall(); err != nil {\n            fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"❌ %v\\n\", err)\n            return err\n        }\n    }\n    // Step 1: pi\n    piPath, piNewlyInstalled, err := EnsurePI()\n    if err != nil {\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"❌ pi is not available and could not be installed: %v\\n\", err)\n        fmt.Fprintf(os.Stderr, \"   Install manually: npm install -g @earendil-works/pi-coding-agent\\n\")\n        return err\n    }\n    ver := PiVersion(piPath)\n    fmt.Printf(\"✅ rick pi runtime ready: %s\", piPath)\n    if ver != \"\" {\n        fmt.Printf(\" (v%s)\", ver)\n    }\n    if piNewlyInstalled {\n        fmt.Printf(\" (newly installed)\")\n    }\n    fmt.Println()\n    // Step 1.5: settings bootstrap\n    if err := BootstrapAgentSettings(); err != nil {\n        ...\n    } else {\n        fmt.Printf(\"✅ pi agent dir ready: %s (hideThinkingBlock=true)\\n\", runtime.AgentDir())\n    }\n    // Step 2: subagent\n    ...\n    // Step 3: web-access\n    ...\n    // Step 4: purge tokyo\n    ...\n    // Step 5: verify\n    ...\n    // 职责3: rick customizations (silent)\n    _ = DeployRickCustomizations()\n    fmt.Println(\"✅ pi environment ready\")\n    return nil\n}\n```\n\nWait, where exactly to put the silent `DeployRickCustomizations()`? Let me put it right before `fmt.Println(\"✅ pi environment ready\")`. Since it's silent, the output is unchanged.\n\nActually, let me reconsider: should I put it before or after \"✅ pi environment ready\"? It doesn't matter for output (silent). I'll put it before the final line so that \"ready\" means everything including customizations is done.\n\nNow, for `pi.go`:\n```go\nfunc PiCommand(args ...string) *exec.Cmd {\n    bin := \"pi\"\n    if rb := runtime.RuntimeBin(); runtime.FileExists(rb) {\n        bin = rb\n    }\n    cmd := exec.Command(bin, args...)\n    cmd.Env = runtime.AgentEnv()\n    return cmd\n}\n\nfunc EnsurePI() (string, bool, error) { ... } // verbatim, uses InstallManagedPI, PiVersion\nfunc InstallManagedPI(version string) error { ... }\nfunc RequireNodeForPiInstall() error { ... }\nfunc PiVersion(piPath string) string { ... }\n```\n\nFor `extensions.go`:\n```go\nvar RequiredExtensions = []string{\"pi-subagents\", \"pi-web-access\"}\n\nfunc VerifyExtensions() []string { ... }\nfunc EnsureNpmExtension(pkg, detect string) error { ... }\nfunc PiListContains(substr string) bool { ... }\n```\n\nFor `settings.go`:\n```go\nconst TokyoNightPkg = \"@wishx127/pi-tokyo-night\"\nvar TokyoNightThemes = []string{\"tokyo-night-dark\", \