{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Now `customizations.go` — `DeployRickCustomizations`. This copies:\n1. rick-gates (from `.rick/skills/rick-gates/`) → `runtime.AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/`\n2. rick skills (`.rick/skills/*_skill/`) → `runtime.AgentDir()/skills/<name>/`\n\nI need to find the source. Use `workspace.GetRickDir()` to find `.rick/skills/`.\n\nLet me write a robust idempotent copy. I'll implement a helper `copyDir(src, dst)` that copies files recursively, creating dirs.\n\nLet me think about the structure of what to copy:\n\nSource `.rick/skills/`:\n- `rick-gates/` (dir with helper.py) → `extensions/rick-gates/`\n- `*_skill/` dirs → `skills/*/`\n\nLet me write:\n```go\nfunc DeployRickCustomizations() error {\n    rickDir, err := workspace.GetRickDir()\n    if err != nil {\n        return fmt.Errorf(\"locate rick dir: %w\", err)\n    }\n    skillsDir := filepath.Join(rickDir, \"skills\")\n    return deployRickCustomizations(skillsDir)\n}\n\nfunc deployRickCustomizations(skillsDir string) error {\n    // rick-gates → extensions/rick-gates/\n    gatesSrc := filepath.Join(skillsDir, \"rick-gates\")\n    if err := copyDirIfExists(gatesSrc, filepath.Join(runtime.AgentDir(), \"extensions\", \"rick-gates\")); err != nil {\n        return err\n    }\n    // *_skill → skills/\n    entries, err := os.ReadDir(skillsDir)\n    if err != nil {\n        if os.IsNotExist(err) { return nil }\n        return err\n    }\n    for _, e := range entries {\n        if !e.IsDir() { continue }\n        // skip rick-gates (deployed to extensions/)\n        if e.Name() == \"rick-gates\" { continue }\n        // only skill dirs (contain skill.md)\n        if !FileExists(filepath.Join(skillsDir, e.Name(), \"skill.md\")) { continue }\n        src := filepath.Join(skillsDir, e.Name())\n        dst := filepath.Join(runtime.AgentDir(), \"skills\", e.Name())\n        if err := copyDir(src, dst); err != nil { return err }\n    }\n    return nil\n}\n```\n\nFor idempotency: copyDir should overwrite files (so re-running updates them). I'll implement copyDir to walk the source and copy each file, overwriting destination. Use `os.ReadFile` + `os.WriteFile` for simplicity, or io.Copy. For small files, ReadFile/WriteFile is fine.\n\nLet me write a `copyDir` that recursively copies. I need to preserve file modes for executables? The rick-gates helper.py and skill helper scripts might be executable. To be safe, preserve mode. Let me use a proper copy with mode preservation.\n\nActually, for simplicity and correctness, let me write:\n```go\nfunc copyDir(src, dst string) error {\n    return filepath.Walk(src, func(path string, info os.FileInfo, err error) error {\n        if err != nil { return err }\n        rel, err := filepath.Rel(src, path)\n        if err != nil { return err }\n        target := filepath.Join(dst, rel)\n        if info.IsDir() {\n            return os.MkdirAll(target, info.Mode().Perm() | 0700) // ensure dir\n        }\n        // copy file\n        data, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n        if err != nil { return err }\n        if err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(target), 0755); err != nil { return err }\n        return os.WriteFile(target, data, info.Mode().Perm())\n    })\n}\n```\n\nHmm, using info.Mode().Perm() for files; for executable scripts (0755) it preserves. For dirs, 0755. Let me just use a fixed mode scheme: dirs 0755, files copy from source mode.\n\nActually, simpler: preserve source file mode via `info.Mode()`. But for a script that's 0755, `info.Mode().Perm()` = 0755. Good. For skill.md (0644), 0644. Good.\n\nLet me also handle the case where source doesn't exist (skip gracefully). For rick-gates, if source missing, skip (don't error), so that `DeployRickCustomizations` doesn't fail when `.rick/skills/rick-gates/` isn't there yet (e.g., running from a repo without it). But wait — for `CheckRickHooks` to pass, helper.py must be deployed. So if source missing, CheckRickHooks would fail. But that's acceptable (the check reports \"not ready\").\n\nActually, the task says \"task3 创建仓库侧 `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py` 占位文件 + 目录骨架\". So I MUST create that file in the repo. Then `DeployRickCustomizations` copies it. Good.\n\nLet me write customizations.go now.\n\nFor the import of workspace, the package path is `github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/workspace`.\n\nLet me write it."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_wjZnhJXkviX3HJjyMYYv3217","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"package env\n\nimport (\n\t\"fmt\"\n\t\"os\"\n\t\"path/filepath\"\n\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/runtime\"\n\t\"github.com/sunquan/rick/internal/workspace\"\n)\n\n// DeployRickCustomizations 落盘 rick 自有定制到 pi 托管 agent 目录（职责 3）：\n//\n//   - rick-gates hook 扩展：<repo>/.rick/skills/rick-gates/ → AgentDir()/extensions/rick-gates/\n//   - rick skills：<repo>/.rick/skills/*_skill/            → AgentDir()/skills/<name>/\n//\n// think/research/exporter agent frontmatter 不在此落盘（task9 经职责 3 写入\n// AgentDir()/agents/），避免本 task 的占位文件被 task9 幂等复制跳过。\n//\n// 幂等：重复运行会重写目标文件（内容一致），不产生重复项。\nfunc DeployRickCustomizations() error {\n\trickDir, err := workspace.GetRickDir()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"locate rick dir: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\treturn deployRickCustomizations(filepath.Join(rickDir, \"skills\"))\n}\n\n// deployRickCustomizations 从给定 skills 源目录复制 rick 定制，便于单测注入临时源目录。\nfunc deployRickCustomizations(skillsDir string) error {\n\t// rick-gates hook 扩展 → extensions/rick-gates/。\n\tif err := copyDir(filepath.Join(skillsDir, \"rick-gates\"),\n\t\tfilepath.Join(runtime.AgentDir(), \"extensions\", \"rick-gates\")); err != nil {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"deploy rick-gates: %w\", err)\n\t}\n\n\t// rick skills（*_skill 目录，含 skill.md）→ skills/。\n\tentries, err := os.ReadDir(skillsDir)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\t\treturn nil // 无 skills 目录 —— 无定制可部署。\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"read skills dir %s: %w\", skillsDir, err)\n\t}\n\tfor _, e := range entries {\n\t\tif !e.IsDir() || e.Name() == \"rick-gates\" {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\t// 仅复制真正的 skill 目录（含 skill.md），跳过 README 等杂项。\n\t\tif !runtime.FileExists(filepath.Join(skillsDir, e.Name(), \"skill.md\")) {\n\t\t\tcontinue\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := copyDir(filepath.Join(skillsDir, e.Name()),\n\t\t\tfilepath.Join(runtime.AgentDir(), \"skills\", e.Name())); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"deploy skill %s: %w\", e.Name(), err)\n\t\t}\n\t}\n\treturn nil\n}\n\n// copyDir 递归复制 src 目录到 dst，保留文件/目录权限。源不存在时返回 nil\n// （幂等 + 容错：部分定制可缺失而不阻断整体部署）。\nfunc copyDir(src, dst string) error {\n\tinfo, err := os.Stat(src)\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tif os.IsNotExist(err) {\n\t\t\treturn nil\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn err\n\t}\n\tif !info.IsDir() {\n\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"%s is not a directory\", src)\n\t}\n\treturn filepath.Walk(src, func(path string, fi os.FileInfo, walkErr error) error {\n\t\tif walkErr != nil {\n\t\t\treturn walkErr\n\t\t}\n\t\trel, err := filepath.Rel(src, path)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\ttarget := filepath.Join(dst, rel)\n\t\tif fi.IsDir() {\n\t\t\treturn os.MkdirAll(target, 0755)\n\t\t}\n\t\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(path)\n\t\tif err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(target), 0755); err != nil {\n\t\t\treturn err\n\t\t}\n\t\tmode := fi.Mode().Perm()\n\t\tif mode == 0 {\n\t\t\tmode = 0644\n\t\t}\n\t\treturn os.WriteFile(target, data, mode)\n\t})\n}\n","path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/env/customizations.go"}}}}
