{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"thinking_end","contentIndex":0,"content":"Wait, there's an issue in `TestRuntimeEnv_Seam`. `pi.DeployCustomizations()` calls `workspace.GetRickDir()` which uses `os.Getwd()`. When running `go test ./internal/env/...`, cwd = `internal/env`. So `workspace.GetRickDir()` returns `internal/env/.rick`, and `deployRickCustomizations(internal/env/.rick/skills)` — skills dir doesn't exist → `os.ReadDir` returns NotExist → returns nil. And copyDir for rick-gates: `internal/env/.rick/skills/rick-gates` doesn't exist → returns nil. So `DeployCustomizations` returns nil. Good.\n\nBut wait — actually `os.ReadDir` on a non-existent dir returns `*PathError` wrapping `syscall.ENOENT`, which `os.IsNotExist` catches. Good.\n\nActually, there's a subtle issue: `copyDir` uses `os.Stat` and returns nil on NotExist. Good.\n\nNow there's another concern: `TestRuntimeEnv_Seam`'s assertion about `DeployCustomizations` returning nil depends on cwd. When run via `go test ./internal/env/...`, cwd is `internal/env`. But it's a bit fragile. Let me make it more robust: instead of relying on cwd, I could `os.Chdir` to a temp dir first. But actually, the test just checks it doesn't error. If cwd happens to have a `.rick/skills` with malformed content... unlikely. Let me keep it but make it more defensive by chdir to a temp dir.\n\nActually, let me simplify `TestRuntimeEnv_Seam` to not depend on cwd. I'll chdir to a temp dir with no `.rick`. Let me rewrite that test.\n\nActually, let me also reconsider: the `DeployRickCustomizations()` called from `Ensure()` (via init-pi) runs from the repo root (cwd = repo root when user runs `rick tools init-pi`). So `.rick/skills/` exists. Good.\n\nBut in the unit test `TestRuntimeEnv_Seam`, I want to avoid cwd dependence. Let me chdir to temp.\n\nLet me update that test."}}
{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"toolcall_end","contentIndex":1,"toolCall":{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_WViJKM3YNd5Xd5M5LtqW4668","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText":"// TestRuntimeEnv_Seam verifies piEnv satisfies RuntimeEnv and its methods\n// dispatch to the package-level functions.\nfunc TestRuntimeEnv_Seam(t *testing.T) {\n\tvar _ RuntimeEnv = NewPiEnv()\n\tpi := NewPiEnv()\n\n\t// 隔离 cwd，使 DeployCustomizations 在无 .rick/skills 源时容错返回 nil。\n\torig, err := os.Getwd()\n\tif err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tempty := t.TempDir()\n\tif err := os.Chdir(empty); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n\t}\n\tdefer func() { _ = os.Chdir(orig) }()\n\tt.Setenv(\"HOME\", t.TempDir())\n\n\tif err := pi.DeployCustomizations(); err != nil {\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"DeployCustomizations should be tolerant, got %v\", err)\n\t}\n\t// CheckReady 汇总四职责，返回未就绪点清单（可能非空，类型正确即可）。\n\t_ = pi.CheckReady()\n}","oldText":"// TestRuntimeEnv_Seam verifies piEnv satisfies RuntimeEnv and its methods\n// dispatch to the package-level functions.\nfunc TestRuntimeEnv_Seam(t *testing.T) {\n\tvar _ RuntimeEnv = NewPiEnv()\n\tpi := NewPiEnv()\n\t// CheckReady 与 DeployCustomizations 无副作用地返回预期类型。\n\tif got := pi.CheckReady(); got == nil {\n\t\tt.Log(\"CheckReady returned nil (ready or missing empty)\")\n\t}\n\tif err := pi.DeployCustomizations(); err != nil {\n\t\t// 无 .rick/skills 源目录时应容错返回 nil，而非报错。\n\t\tt.Errorf(\"DeployCustomizations should be tolerant, got %v\", err)\n\t}\n}"}],"path":"/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/internal/env/env_test.go"}}}}
