{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Wait, there's an issue in `TestRuntimeEnv_Seam`. `pi.DeployCustomizations()` calls `workspace.GetRickDir()` which uses `os.Getwd()`. When running `go test ./internal/env/...`, cwd = `internal/env`. So `workspace.GetRickDir()` returns `internal/env/.rick`, and `deployRickCustomizations(internal/env/.rick/skills)` — skills dir doesn't exist → `os.ReadDir` returns NotExist → returns nil. And copyDir for rick-gates: `internal/env/.rick/skills/rick-gates` doesn't exist → returns nil. So `DeployCustomizations` returns nil. Good.\n\nBut wait — actually `os.ReadDir` on a non-existent dir returns `*PathError` wrapping `syscall.ENOENT`, which `os.IsNotExist` catches. Good.\n\nActually, there's a subtle issue: `copyDir` uses `os.Stat` and returns nil on NotExist. Good.\n\nNow there's another concern: `TestRuntimeEnv_Seam`'s assertion about `DeployCustomizations` returning nil depends on cwd. When run via `go test ./internal/env/...`, cwd is `internal/env`. But it's a bit fragile. Let me make it more robust: instead of relying on cwd, I could `os.Chdir` to a temp dir first. But actually, the test just checks it doesn't error. If cwd happens to have a `.rick/skills` with malformed content... unlikely. Let me keep it but make it more defensive by chdir to a temp dir.\n\nActually, let me simplify `TestRuntimeEnv_Seam` to not depend on cwd. I'll chdir to a temp dir with no `.rick`. Let me rewrite that test.\n\nActually, let me also reconsider: the `DeployRickCustomizations()` called from `Ensure()` (via init-pi) runs from the repo root (cwd = repo root when user runs `rick tools init-pi`). So `.rick/skills/` exists. Good.\n\nBut in the unit test `TestRuntimeEnv_Seam`, I want to avoid cwd dependence. Let me chdir to temp.\n\nLet me update that test.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_WViJKM3YNd5Xd5M5LtqW4668","name":"edit","arguments":{"edits":[{"newText