{"type":"turn_end","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now there might be a subtle issue: `TestExecuteDoingWorkflow_ResumesFromTasksJSON` and `TestExecuteDoingWorkflow_WithMockPi` set PATH with the mock \"pi\" prepended. But they set `t.Setenv(\"HOME\", dir)` already (for config), so RuntimeBin won't resolve to real pi. With mock \"pi\" on PATH first, `exec.Command(\"pi\", ...)` → fake pi exits 0 → parseStream gets empty → returns nil session. Good.\n\nBut wait — does the fake pi need to handle `--mode json` and produce output? No. The executor calls `parseStream` on stdout which will immediately EOF (fake pi produces no output and exits 0). So parseStream returns sess with empty fields, no error. Then GenerateTestWithAgent checks for test script creation — not created → task fails → retry.\n\nActually wait, let me check what `parseStream` does on empty stream — does it error? Let me check executor.go parseStream.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_N7HRR5sEMKrkpmdlEbWZ9038","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && sed -n '120,260p' internal/runtime/executor.go"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":178,"output":288,"cacheRead":173184,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":213,"totalTokens":173650,"cost":{"input":0.00007743000000000001,"output":0.00025056,"cacheRead":0.0006277920000000001,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.0009557820000000001}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786906452982,"responseId":"58251d21-ff3b-4052-9d54-024bd601e7d1","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},"toolResults":[{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_N7HRR5sEMKrkpmdlEbWZ9038","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\ntype piSession struct {\n\tsessionID        string\n\ttoolCalls        []agent.ToolCall\n\ttoolCallIDs      []string // parallel to toolCalls, for matching end→start by toolCallId\n\tfinalMessage     string\n\tfinalMe