 the doing_check would run the OLD code. But doing_check is just format validation (tasks.json + debug/), which doesn't depend on my env changes. Still, for correctness, I should rebuild bin/rick with my changes so the check runs the latest.\n\nActually, the task prompt's Step 2 (format check) says: `/workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick/bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`. So I should rebuild bin/rick with my changes, then run doing_check.\n\nBut wait — should I commit the rebuilt bin/rick? The convention is unclear. Looking at the git history: `git log --oneline -5 -- bin/rick` earlier showed recent commits touching bin/rick (release commits). For feature tasks, they typically DON'T commit bin/rick (it's rebuilt separately). Let me check: did task4/task5 commit bin/rick? \n\ntask4 log L40413: \"git ls-files bin/rick && ... git log --oneline -3 -- bin/rick\". Let me check what task4/task5 committed for bin/rick.\n\nActually, let me just check the git log for bin/rick to understand the convention."}}
