me -> Dracula palette\na1bccd8 style(job_34): rick theme -> geek/hacker palette (Matrix green on near-black)\n782f331 revert(job_34): remove pi runtime patching - keep theme config + self-contained runtime only\n740756d feat(job_34): rick patch-pi - edit-diff + bash command syntax highlighting\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786906540932},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"`bin/rick` is only committed on release/style commits (job_34 theme work). For feature tasks (task4/task5), they did NOT commit bin/rick (the feature commits didn't touch bin/rick). So I should NOT commit bin/rick. But I SHOULD rebuild it so the doing_check runs the latest code.\n\nLet me rebuild bin/rick (for the check) but not commit it. Actually, since `bin/rick` is already modified (stale from a previous build), rebuilding it with my changes is fine — it'll still be \"M\" in git status, and I'll just not `git add` it.\n\nActually, wait — I want to be careful. The `bin/rick` is currently at 8368560 bytes (pre-task3 build). If I rebuild with my changes, it'll be a new size. Either way it's \"M\" (uncommitted). I'll rebuild it to ensure the check uses my latest code, and NOT commit it (consistent with task4/task5 which didn't commit bin/rick).\n\nLet me rebuild bin/rick and run doing_check.\n\nActually, let me reconsider. The doing_check just validates tasks.json + debug/. My env changes don't affect doing_check. But to be safe and follow the task's Step 2 instruction (`bin/rick tools doing_check job_35`), I'll rebuild bin/rick with my changes and run it.\n\nLet me rebuild and run doing_check.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_h9QtWXhoWaGRMhBgnSsW9202","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && go build -o bin/rick ./cmd/rick && ./bin/rick tools doing_check job_35 2>&1; echo \"exit=$?\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":249,"output":398,"cacheRead":181376,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":307,"totalTokens":182023,"cost":{"input":0.00010831500000000001,"output":0.00034626000000000004,"cacheRead":0.000657488,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.001112063}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786906540934,"responseId":"ab2dbf46-c6c4-43f8-964c-590cbd9a5c67","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_h9QtWXhoWaGRMhBgnSsW9202","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"❌ doing check failed: task task3 is in zombie 'running' state — change to 'failed' if stuck\nexit=1\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786906548556},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The doing_check failed because task3 is in \"running\" state (zombie detection). I need to mark it. The task is currently \"running\" (I'm executing it). The doing_check expects tasks to be in a valid state (not \"running\" zombie).\n\nThis is the zombie check. The `mark_task_success.py` skill will mark task3 as \"success\" with commit hash. But first I need to commit my changes, then run mark_task_success.\n\nActually, let me look at the flow: \n1. Commit my feat changes.\n2. Run mark_task_success.py to mark task3 success (requires commit hash).\n3. Commit the tasks.json change.\n4. Run doing_check.\n\nBut the zombie check requires the task NOT be \"running\" (or \"failed\"). Since I'm actively working on it, it's \"running\". After I commit and mark success, it'll be \"success\" and pass.\n\nLet me check the mark_task_success skill to understand the flow.\n\nActually, wait — let me re-read the doing_check error: \"task task3 is in zombie 'running' state — change to 'failed' if stuck\". This is a zombie detection in the check. It flags \"running\" tasks as zombie. To pass doing_check, task3 must be \"success\" or \"failed\".\n\nSo the flow is: commit my work, then mark task3 success (which sets status=\"success\" + commit_hash), then doing_check passes.\n\nLet me first commit my feat changes. Let me stage only my files.\n\nFiles to stage:\n- `internal/env/` (new dir)\n- `internal/cmd/tools_init_pi.go`\n- `internal/cmd/tools_init_pi_test.go` (deleted)\n- `internal/cmd/tools_theme.go`\n- `internal/cmd/tools_theme_test.go`\n- `internal/cmd/doing_test.go`\n- `internal/cmd/learning_test.go`\n- `internal/cmd/themes/` (renames to env/themes)\n- `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py`\n\nLet me check the mark_task_success skill first to understand exactly what it does and what it needs.","thinkingSignature":"reasoning_content"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_5VAZ9OcehTGlbIVS9FkO1799","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"cd /workdir/sunquan20/AI_CODING/rick && cat .rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/skill.md 2>/dev/null | head -80"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"deepseek","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":48,"output":542,"cacheRead":182016,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":458,"totalTokens":182606,"cost":{"input":0.00002088,"output":0.00047154,"cacheRead":0.000659808,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.001152228}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1786906548559,"responseId":"846a30f4-1cfd-44ed-914c-ba935d22800c","rawStopReason":"tool_calls"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_5VAZ9OcehTGlbIVS9FkO1799","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# skill:mark-task-success（tasks.json 两阶段提交）\n\n## 触发场景\n\ndoing task 代码已提交（有 commit hash）但 doing_check 报错：\n- `task status != success`\n- `task status=success but commit_hash is empty`\n\n信号词：`doing_check` 输出 `task status` 相关错误。\n\n## 预期效果\n\n- 一次修复通过 doing_check\n- 不需要反复读取 tasks.json 格式或 check 源码\n\n## 核心内容\n\n### 使用辅助脚本（推荐）\n\n```bash\n# 代码已 commit 后，立即执行：\npython3 .rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/mark_task_success.py --job job_N --task taskX\n# 工具自动读取 HEAD commit hash，更新 tasks.json status=success + commit_hash\n\n# 提交 tasks.json：\ngit add .rick/jobs/job_N/doing/tasks.json\ngit commit -m \"chore(taskX): mark taskX success in tasks.json\"\n\n# 验证：\n./bin/rick tools doing_check job_N  # 应输出 ✅ PASS\n```\n\n### 手动修复（备用）\n\n```python\nimport json, subprocess\n\n# 获取 commit hash\nhash_result = subprocess.run([\"git\", \"rev-parse\", \"HEAD\"], capture_output=True, text=True)\ncommit_hash = hash_result.stdout.strip()\n\n# 更新 tasks.json\nwith open(\".rick/jobs/job_N/doing/tasks.json\", \"r\") as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\nfor task in data[\"tasks\"]:\n    if task[\"task_id\"] == \"taskX\":\n        task[\"status\"] = \"success\"\n        task[\"commit_hash\"] = commit_hash\n        break\n\nwith open(\".rick/jobs/job_N/doing/tasks.json\", \"w\") as f:\n    json.dump(data, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\n```\n\n### 最优执行序（避免二次失败）\n\n1. 完成代码变更 → `git commit` → 记录 commit hash\n2. `python3 .rick/skills/mark_task_success_skill/mark_task_success.py --job job_N --task taskX`\n3. `git add tasks.json && git commit -m \"chore(taskX): mark success\"`\n4. `./bin/rick tools doing_check job_N`（此时必过）\n\n### tasks.json 结构说明\n\n```json\n{\n  \"tasks\": [\n    {\n      \"task_id\": \"task1\",\n      \"status\": \"success\",\n      \"commit_hash\": \"40位SHA\",\n      \"updated_at\": \"2026-07-02T...\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n`status=success` + `commit_hash` 非空 → doing_check 通过。\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1786906556742},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I understand the flow. Let me:\n1. Stage and commit my feat changes.\n2. Run mark_task_success.py.\n3. Commit tasks.json.\n4. Run doing_check.\n\nLet me stage my files carefully. I'll use `git add` with explicit paths.\n\nFiles:\n- `internal/env/` (new)\n- `internal/cmd/tools_init_pi.go`\n- `internal/cmd/tools_init_pi_test.go` (deleted - use `git add` with the path to stage deletion)\n- `internal/cmd/tools_theme.go`\n- `internal/cmd/tools_theme_test.go`\n- `internal/cmd/doing_test.go`\n- `internal/cmd/learning_test.go`\n- `internal/cmd/themes/` (renames)\n- `.rick/skills/rick-gates/helper.py`\n\nFor the renames (R), `git add internal/cmd/themes internal/env/themes` will stage them. Actually since I used `mv` (n